{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And the ears swallowed them.</b> One may say they grew upward and covered the first ones so that they were not seen — in the sense of <b>בלע</b> like <i>בלע את הקדש</i> (consecrated objects absorbed). And one should not explain it as literal swallowing, for a person is not shown something impossible, such as an elephant passing through the eye of a needle." "<b>And behold a dream.</b> Because all the while a person sleeps, the dream seems to him to be an actual event and true, and when he wakes he realizes it was a dream, as it is written: ״והיה כאשר יחלום הצמא והנה שותה והקיץ ונפשו שוקקה״. And even in the dream of the cows it should have said likewise, except he waited until he finished speaking. And one may say: regarding the cows it does not write <b>והנה חלום</b>, because it can happen that animals eat one another, but regarding ears of grain it is not applicable to say so; therefore he wrote about them <b>והנה חלום</b> — surely this vision is not [merely] a dream. Another interpretation: <b>והנה חלום</b> — now the dream was concluded; he did not dream any more about the matter."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:08:13.889878507Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}